  "spiritual_reading": "\n\n\n# Spiritual Translation of the Kephalaia Chapter on the Two Trees\n\n---\n\n**¶5.** Great is the teaching that proceeds from the Divine itself… The fragmented falsities of those who divide truth against itself… Yet concerning what they explain about the two perceptions — the perception rooted in wisdom and the perception rooted in falsity — as they reckon them… these perceptions, as they arise within the composite natural mind, which mingles good and evil together… Consider the particular perception they examine: not every derivative of a single perception leads to genuine understanding, for not every extension of it can be put to spiritual use.\n\n**¶6.** …that which proceeds from them, as it impresses itself upon the mind… while at first one aspect appears… yet at last there remains one quality… it manifests in the derivative truths and the extending branches of that perception… There is a falsified residue within them, a dead dust clinging to the derivatives of perception… before the perception that… is corrupted; because they render judgment… the one they designate… the kind… they name it: a perception… what is inwardly delightful… what is written in doctrine… they shall establish… the human mind… it delights the will… the interior truth of… and it is taken up for spiritual nourishment… will make known… may not be conjoined to… those of the human race, as they are called…\n\n**¶11.** …how I will disclose to you… the one who unfolds the interior meaning… the perceptions… the Divine itself… all of them, as He… in the… created order… this perception rooted in wisdom, the… the wisdom shining within this good perception… the Divine Truth standing forth…\n\n**¶12.** …the wisdoms that are clothed upon the external form of this good perception. They are the elements of wisdom that have been dispersed and interwoven throughout the whole of creation.\n\n**¶14.** Behold, this is the perception rooted in wisdom.\n\n**¶15.** I disclose to you its nature: it has five faculties. They are consideration, counsel, insight, thought, and mind. Its *consideration* is the spiritual community that receives good and truth — the holy church. Its *counsel* is the Divine Truth made manifest, the Divine Human in its perfected form. Its *insight* is the Divine Human principle dwelling within the doctrine of living truth. Its *thought* is the Divine Proceeding dwelling within the doctrine of Divine Love, which shines forth in radiance. And its *mind* is the Divine Itself, dwelling in supreme greatness, perfect among the eternal states of wisdom.\n\n**¶17.** It is through consideration that souls first receive; they are raised upward. Then they are raised to counsel — the Divine Truth made manifest. From counsel they are raised to insight, which is the Divine Human dwelling in the doctrine that carries through states of obscurity. From insight they rise to thought, which is the Divine Proceeding dwelling in the doctrine that carries through states of full illumination. And this great and glorious thought — the highest proceeding activity — brings them inward at last to mind, which is the Divine Itself, the God of truth, the inmost Wisdom of all the eternal states of glory.\n\n**¶18.** This is the perception rooted in wisdom that produces good works. It is the fullness of love and wisdom forever. It is blessed eternally.\n\n**¶19.** …the corrupted perception… that which arises within… from… also… the manner in which… the perception rooted in wisdom… contrasted with that of self-love… they are the dominions of self-love… the perverted spiritual order and the turning cycle of compulsions… they are the five corporeal appetites that move and act… the works they produce… the doctrine of error, the hidden falsity that the ruling evil established within the world.\n\n**¶20.** The appropriation of these evil works is made by those who are evil — the fragmented falsities, the sects, who are bound under one external compulsion after another, they and those who propagate their falsity, under the rule of spiritual death. They take this as their sustenance; they thirst for it. They become minds given wholly to spiritual death.\n\n**¶22.** I will disclose to you: the perception rooted in falsity has five faculties. They are consideration, counsel, insight, thought, and mind. Its *consideration* is the rule of spiritual death, from which the fragmented falsities draw all their instruction. Its *counsel* is the passage from one state of falsity into another, through form after form, endlessly revolving. Its *insight* is the consuming punishment of self-love — the devastation that is filled with the dense obscurity of compounded falsity. Its *thought* is a containing form that holds evil within it. Its *mind* is the consolidated mass of evil, the final bond from which there is no release — that which the ruling evil cast away into the outermost… and they fall… into utter falsity… all that remains is taken away… they are swallowed into the mass of consolidated evil, and they are bound within the works of falsity, those works that belong to it forever and ever… no face turned toward the Divine… whoever arrives at that state has no possibility of reformation within it.\n\n**¶23.** This is the unfolding of the perception rooted in falsity, as I have set it forth — which you must distinguish from the good works of the other. That perception cannot bring forth good works; its works are entirely evil, throughout all the days of its existence.\n\n**¶24.** Concerning this… and those whom I love… them in truth — the one perception being transformed from its opposite… the perception rooted in wisdom, which lies in the good ground of the natural mind, is love and wisdom entire; spiritual death and falsity have no existence within it. And the perception rooted in falsity is the merely corporeal and material… I understand it as standing utterly alone and apart… which exists within the corrupted ground of the natural mind… it is falsity and spiritual death.\n\n**¶25.** Blessed is every one who can distinguish these two perceptions and separate them one from the other. He understands that they did not arise out of one another, nor did they proceed from one another. They did not come from a single origin. The person who can separate them may ascend to the eternal state of wisdom, as I have disclosed it to you.\n\n**¶26.** And he sees clearly that evil works did not arise from the perception of wisdom. But whoever cannot separate the one from the other falls into the realm of falsity, until he arrives at the uttermost state.\n\n**¶27.** Blessed is whoever can receive this in faith. He is freed from the falsity that grows out of the darkness, forever and ever.",
  "reconstructions": [
    {
      "paragraph": 5,
      "reconstructed_text": "Great is [the teaching that the Father has spoken] by his own mouth [concerning the good and the] bad [trees.] The sects [have spoken falsely of them.] Yet, this that they explain about the two trees, as they reckon them, [they set] the trees [forth] in an explanation [that is not fitting;] because [the] tree, as it grows on this composite earth, [take for example the] date palm, because [not all of it is good], for not absolutely every part of the date palm is used!"
    },
    {
      "paragraph": 6,
      "reconstructed_text": "[Consider] their child, as it strikes [root;] while first one [part appears good] in them [, yet] at the end there is one [part that is bad;] it occurs in its fibres and its branches [and its thorns.] There is a bad dust in them [, in the] date palm [. Look] before the tree that [is] bad; because they give the decision [concerning] the one that they name [good, and] the type [they] name it: tree [of life. Its fruit] is sweet [. In the] writing [of the scriptures] they shall establish [that the] man [who eats of it finds] it is sweet [. The] seed of the [tree,] and it is used for their nourishment [. Yet they] will explain [that one] may not join to the [bad tree. And] mankind, as they are named [, shall discern between them.]"
    },
    {
      "paragraph": 11,
      "reconstructed_text": "[Now hear] how I will reveal to you [the truth. I am] the expound[er of the mystery of] the trees [.] the Father [of greatness has established] all of them, as he [has set them] in the [entire] world [. Now] this good tree, the [light that is in it:] the light of this good tree [is] the Pillar [of Glory.]"
    },
    {
      "paragraph": 12,
      "reconstructed_text": "[They are] the intellectuals that are cloaked upon its body [, the body of] this good tree. They are the light elements that are mingled, being compounded in the totality."
    },
    {
      "paragraph": 14,
      "reconstructed_text": "Behold, this is the good tree [that I have explained to you.]"
    },
    {
      "paragraph": 15,
      "reconstructed_text": "[Now] I reveal to you [its nature:] it has five limbs. [They are consideration, counsel, insight, thought, mind.] Its consideration is the holy church. [Its counsel] is the Pillar of Glory, the Perfect Man. [Its insight is the Fir]st Man who dwells in the ship of living waters. Its thought is the Third Ambassador [who dwells in] the ship of living fire, that shines in [the heavens.] Also, the mind is the Father who dwells in greatness, who is perfect in the aeons of light."
    },
    {
      "paragraph": 17,
      "reconstructed_text": "It is consideration that shall [first receive the souls, and] they shall be raised up [to that which] is counsel; they shall be raised up to insight, which is the First Man who dwells in the ship of the night; from insight they shall rise up to thought, which is the Ambassador who dwells in the ship of the day. And he too, great glorious thought, shall bring them in to mind; which is the Father, the God of truth, the great Mind of all the aeons of glory."
    },
    {
      "paragraph": 18,
      "reconstructed_text": "This is the good tree that shall give good fruit, [which] is the entire life and light for ever [. Whatever] occurs [in it for] ever, it is blessed [for ever and ever.]"
    },
    {
      "paragraph": 19,
      "reconstructed_text": "[Now I shall tell you concerning the] bad [tree, and what shall] happen in [the world] from [it.] also [consider] the way that it is [set against] the good tree [. The realms] of the fire [and the smoke,] they are the ruling-power [of] heaven and the wheel [of the zodiac;] they are the five fleshes that walk [upon the earth. The] fruit [of this bad tree is the te]aching as of error, the mystery that [the ruler of darkness brought forth, wh]ich Satan appointed in the world."
    },
    {
      "paragraph": 20,
      "reconstructed_text": "However, the taste of these bad fruits is these evil people, the sects [of the world, wh]ich are bound in law after law, they and their teachers [who lead them in] the law of death; they taking taste for it, they being thirsty for it [, and they become] the souls of death."
    },
    {
      "paragraph": 22,
      "reconstructed_text": "[Now I will] reveal to you and you [shall understand.] The bad tree has five limbs. They are consideration, counsel, insight, thought, mind. Its consideration is the law of death from which the sects take instruction. Its counsel is transmigration [, the passage from form to form,] in type after type. Also, its insight is the furnaces of fire [and ge]henna; which is full of smoke. Thought [is the containing] vessel. Its mind is the [depth of] the lump, the last bond, the [final prison], they that Satan cast away [into the outermost darkness, into] the great [abyss;] and they fall [into] the darkness [.] all [that is good in them,] and they take away [the light from them. They] are swallowed in to the lump, and they are bound [in] the fruit of darkness, the one that they [bear] for ever and ever [. No more shall] his face [turn to the light; whoever] will arrive at that place; and they have no repentance therein."
    },
    {
      "paragraph": 24,
      "reconstructed_text": "Concerning this [teaching, my catechumens] and my beloved ones [shall know] them in truth, it being changed from [its opposite. The good tree is that] which lies in its good earth [, which is life] and light; as death and darkness do not exist [in it.] Also, the bad tree is Matter [; and concerning] it, I understand it alone among the [two. That wh]ich occurs in its bad earth [is] darkness and death."
    },
    {
      "paragraph": 25,
      "reconstructed_text": "Blessed is every one [who can understand] these two trees, and separates them one from another. He understands that they did not arise out of one another, nor did they come from one another. They did not come from one! The person who can separate them out may go up to the aeon of light, [even as I have] revealed it to you."
    },
    {
      "paragraph": 26,
      "reconstructed_text": "And he sees [that the] bad fruit did not arise from it [, from the good tree]; but whoever will not separate out [the one] from one another, he falls to the land of darkness [for ever,] until he arrives at the [lump of darkness.]"
    },
    {
      "paragraph": 27,
      "reconstructed_text": "Blessed is whoever can believe! He [shall be freed from] darkness; which grows out of the [bad earth] for ever and ever."
    },
    {
      "paragraph": 23,
      "reconstructed_text": "[Now behold,] this is the explanation of the bad tree, as I have explained to you, which you [shall not ascribe] to it [any] good fruit [; for] its fruit bad [is all that is] in it, in its existent days [; there is no good] in it."
    }
